  "bare_pub_baseline_2026_08_23": "2026-08-23: bare_pub_non_lib 13699 -> 13703. Seven bare pubs landed on 2026-08-22 and two were removed; of the seven, ONE was narrowable and was narrowed rather than absorbed (ElabCtx::set_unstaged_siblings -> pub(crate); its only caller is crate::module_batch::exec). The remaining four are structurally required and are the whole of this +4: (1) clean-elab infer::UnstagedSibling -- named in lib.rs's `pub use infer::{..}` list, so pub(crate) would not compile; (2) clean-kernel LocalContext::reserve_fvar_floor -- called ACROSS crates from clean-elab infer::demand_local_ctx; (3,4) clean-lake InitArgs::exe_project / ::lib_project -- consumed by the tests/parity_battery integration test THROUGH the crate lib, the same shape as the +2 recorded at 736193d31. files_over_500 was NOT bumped: its +10 was fixed by splitting, and it is back at the 1424 it has held since 736193d31.",
  "files_over_1000_baseline_2026_08_28": "2026-08-28: files_over_1000 441 -> 442, and it is NOT this commit's. `crates/clean-elab/src/codata_variant_coind.rs` crossed at 1026 lines in 3886de0da (codata VC-6), and origin/main was measured RED on this counter at be87f72e1 BEFORE the simp-emitter commit rebased onto it — so a lane pushed past an uninstalled or bypassed hook (CLAUDE.md records that 59 of 61 worktrees still carry the old scripts/hooks/pre-push). Absorbed here as a RECORD, not an endorsement: the file is the codata lane's active work and splitting it mid-flight would conflict with them. The right fix is theirs, and it is a module split, not a baseline. unwrap_expect_production 1230 -> 1229 is likewise not this commit's: it measured -1 identically with and without these changes."
